{%- doc -%}
  The small name-and-price label on a home hero photo (docs/home-hero-plan.md §5). The price is the product's own,
  so it can't go stale. Renders nothing without a product. It sits inside the photo's link and becomes its name,
  so the photo's alt text is left empty when this shows. Prices drop ".00" so the name has room on a phone.
  A long name and price ("Sunflower bouquet", "From ₹169") don't fit one line on a phone's photo, so there the
  price goes under the name instead of the name breaking in two beside it.

  @param {product} product - The product in the photo
  @param {string} [label] - A short name for the label. Defaults to the product's title.

  @example
  {% render 'hero-tag', product: block.settings.product, label: block.settings.label %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign tag_name = label | default: product.title
    if product.price_varies
      assign min_price = product.price_min | money_without_trailing_zeros
      assign tag_price = 'products.from_price' | t: price: min_price
    else
      assign tag_price = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
    endif
    # About 22 characters fit beside each other on the 218px photo of a 360px phone.
    assign tag_chars = tag_price | strip_html | size | plus: tag_name.size
  -%}
  <span class="hero__tag{% if tag_chars > 22 %} hero__tag--stack{% endif %}"><span class="hero__tag-name">{{ tag_name | escape }}</span> <span class="hero__tag-price">{{ tag_price }}</span></span>
{%- endif -%}
